From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:01:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] icu: <typeinfo> with default visibility before gcc_hidden.h
 (GCC 12, ARM EABI; T-633)

ICU is built without the STL wrappers under gcc_hidden.h's push(hidden).
GCC 12's libstdc++ declares std::type_info::operator== out of line on ARM
EABI, so numfmt.cpp's typeid comparisons referenced it as a hidden undefined
symbol and gold refused libxul. A force-included header declares <typeinfo>
first, with default visibility; GCC 9's inline operator== is unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MpagfP34fXBdsc76E8YSzR
---
 config/external/icu/defs.mozbuild      |  2 ++
 config/external/icu/typeinfo-default.h | 14 ++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 config/external/icu/typeinfo-default.h

diff --git a/config/external/icu/defs.mozbuild b/config/external/icu/defs.mozbuild
index b1ea56455c..9d971323d8 100644
--- a/config/external/icu/defs.mozbuild
+++ b/config/external/icu/defs.mozbuild
@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@ if CONFIG['MOZ_DEBUG']:
 # ICU requires RTTI
 if CONFIG['GNU_CXX']:
     CXXFLAGS += ['-frtti']
+    # Jihad (T-633): <typeinfo> with default visibility before gcc_hidden.h's push(hidden) applies (GCC 12, ARM EABI)
+    CXXFLAGS += ['-include', '%s/config/external/icu/typeinfo-default.h' % TOPSRCDIR]
 elif CONFIG['OS_TARGET'] == 'WINNT':
     CXXFLAGS += ['-GR']
 
diff --git a/config/external/icu/typeinfo-default.h b/config/external/icu/typeinfo-default.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..c6b49f1470
--- /dev/null
+++ b/config/external/icu/typeinfo-default.h
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+/* This Source Code Form is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public
+ * License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
+ * file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/. */
+
+/* Jihad (T-633): force-included into ICU, which is built without the STL wrappers (DISABLE_STL_WRAPPING) under
+ * gcc_hidden.h's "visibility push(hidden)". GCC 12's libstdc++ declares std::type_info::operator== out of line on
+ * ARM EABI, so ICU's typeid comparisons (numfmt.cpp) referenced it as a HIDDEN undefined symbol and gold refused the
+ * link ("hidden symbol '_ZNKSt9type_infoeqERKS_' is not defined locally"). Declared here first, with default
+ * visibility, as every wrapped file already sees it. GCC 9's inline operator== is unaffected. */
+#if defined(__cplusplus) && defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__clang__)
+#pragma GCC visibility push(default)
+#include <typeinfo>
+#pragma GCC visibility pop
+#endif
